-These fields drive the data quality indicator shown in the statistical catalog browser UI (when built) and are available via `GET /api/admin/table-builder/tables`.
+Catalog verification is independent of observation availability. A verified table
+with no stored observations reports `false` / `NO DATA`; an unverified table with
+stored observations reports `true` / `REAL DATA`. In-memory fallback tables report
+`false` / `NO DATA` because they do not establish persisted data availability.
+
+These fields are available via `GET /api/admin/table-builder/tables` and the table-detail/catalog services. They indicate data presence, not approval, accuracy, or permission to publish. The API-wide field reports observations for the table, not a selected dataset.
 
